### Description

I am using the latest version of `langgraph (0.6.0)` which introduced the new 
context API with runtime context injection.

I have created a graph which is connected to multiple subgraphs. The runtime 
context is same in all of those graphs and subgraphs. When I pass the context to
the graph invocation at the top level, I expect that the runtime context will be
available in the subgraph node as well - similar to how the 
`config['configurable']` was available prior to this. However, that doesn't 
happen.

In addition to the minimal example added here, the runtime context is also not 
passed if I use `Send` to dynamically invoke subgraph multiple times.

